## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of streaming distinct-count with memory constraints and practical trade-offs between accuracy and memory.

## Key Concepts
- HyperLogLog sketch
- register count m controls error
- per-element O(1) update, O(m) memory, mergeable sketches

## Code Example
```javascript
class HyperLogLog {
  constructor(m = 16) {
    this.m = m; this.registers = new Uint8Array(m);
  }
  hash(x) {
    let h = 2166136261;
    for (let i = 0; i < x.length; i++) h = (h ^ x.charCodeAt(i)) * 16777619 >>> 0;
    return h;
  }
  add(x) {
    const h = this.hash(x);
    const idx = h & (this.m - 1);
    const w = h >>> Math.log2(this.m);
    const leading = Math.clz32(w) + 1;
    this.registers[idx] = Math.max(this.registers[idx], leading);
  }
  estimate() {
    let sum = 0;
    for (const r of this.registers) sum += Math.pow(2, -r);
    const alpha = 0.7213 / (1 + 1.079 / this.m);
    return alpha * this.m * this.m / sum;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How does choosing m affect relative error and memory? 
- How would you merge two sketches in a distributed setup? 
- What pitfalls exist with non-uniform ID distributions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests streaming algorithm intuition and amortized reasoning. Detecting heavy hitters with bounded memory on a growing stream is a common interview topic; Misra–Gries provides deterministic guarantees with simple updates.

## Key Concepts
- Misra–Gries heavy-hitters
- Choice of k = floor(1/phi) + 1 to bound missed items
- Amortized O(1) per element, O(k) memory
- Trade-offs: larger k reduces false positives but uses more memory

## Code Example
```javascript
class MGHeavyHitters {
  constructor(k) {
    this.k = k;
    this.counters = new Map();
  }
  update(x) {
    if (this.counters.has(x)) {
      this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x) + 1);
      return;
    }
    if (this.counters.size < this.k) {
      this.counters.set(x, 1);
      return;
    }
    for (const [key, val] of Array.from(this.counters)) {
      if (val === 1) this.counters.delete(key);
      else this.counters.set(key, val - 1);
    }
  }
  candidates() { return Array.from(this.counters.keys()); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the phi-bound with a second pass or a secondary sketch in production?
- How does batch size B influence practical update throughput and memory usage?

